.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Landmarks derived from third-party footage. Kept out of the repo because the source
# videos carry their own licenses; see temporal/SOURCES.md for how to regenerate it.
temporal/external_clips.npz

# Your own recordings and the models trained from them ARE meant to be committed --
# collect_motion.py stores landmarks rather than JPEGs precisely so that stays cheap
# (a few hundred KB, against the 650 MB of images in RandomForest/data).

# Generated by docs/export_models.py alongside models.json; GitHub Pages compresses the plain
# .json on the fly, so committing the .gz beside it would buy nothing. models.json itself stays
# committed as the readable reference even though the page now fetches the binary pair instead.
# Kept local for the gzip test.
# (Pages compresses it on the fly at about level 5: `gzip -5 -c docs/models.json` is 3,703,069 B
# here and the deployed site returns 3,703,057 B, against 3,461,703 B at level 9, which is what
# export_models.py writes.)
docs/models.json.gz

# The raw binary sidecar, also from docs/export_models.py. Unlike the JSON, its .gz IS
# committed, and is the file the page fetches (app.js: loadModels('./models.bin.gz',
# './models.meta.json')): GitHub Pages compresses text media types on the fly but leaves
# application/octet-stream alone, so serving this raw file would put 2,555,774 B on the wire
# where docs/models.bin.gz puts 1,183,438 B (measured on the committed export).
# docs/models.meta.json (2,726 B: class lists, feature tags, thresholds, section offsets) and
# docs/parity.json (1,062 B, from docs/parity_probes.py) are small and
# are committed beside it; both are bound to the .bin by its build id, so all three move
# together or docs/test_forest.mjs says so.
docs/models.bin

# Diagnostics the local dev server writes when the page posts to /log.
docs/browser_log.jsonl

# Written by docs/make_demo.sh beside the committed GIF. It is the asset to drag into a
# GitHub editor for an inline player; the repo itself ships the GIF.
docs/demo.mp4

# The Google Books 1-gram counts docs/build_words.py and temporal/simulate_words.py read
# (1.5 MB, CC BY 3.0; fetched with curl -L from norvig.com). The derived docs/words.txt is
# what ships.
docs/google-books-common-words.txt
# ingest_aslnow.py's download cache; the derived temporal/aslnow.npz is what ships.
temporal/.aslnow_cache/
